PERMISSION IS NOT REQUIRED FOR EUROPEAN CARRIES TO OPERATE COMMERCIAL AIR SERVICES INSIDE EU + EFTA (DWITZERLAND, LICHTENSTEIN, NORWAY AND ICELAND)
NOT POSSIBLE TO OBTAIN PERMISSION OR CLEARANCE FROM CAA OR FMP OUTSIDE WORKING HOURS                 IN CASE COMMERCIAL FLIGHT COMES FROM A THIRD-WORLD COUNTRY (BELARUS,RUSSIA,AFRICA,ETC..)

PERMISSION IS NOT REQUIRED FOR PRIVATE, TECHNICAL flights!                                                                                       THE CATEGORIES OF THE NON-SCHEDULED FLIGHTS, FOR WHICH PERMIT OF  OF LITHUANIA ARE NOT NEEDED: 
1.FLIGHT OF THE EMERGENCY MEDICAL ASSISTANCE; 
2. FLIGHT OF A EU MEMBER – STATE AIR CARRIER BY THE AIRCRAFT,WHICH THE MAXIMUM TAKE-OFF WEIGHT (MTOM) IS UNDER 5700 KG AND WHICH IN COMPLIANCE WITH THE TECHNICAL DOCUMENTS CAN CARRY NOT MORE THAN 10 PASSENGERS OR IT CARRIES CARGO ON BOARD (TAXY FLIGHT); 
3. NON-SCHEDULED COMMERCIAL FLIGHT OF A EU MEMBER – STATE AIR CARRIER IN COMPLIANCE WITH THE COUNCIL REGULATION (EEC) NO 2408/92 OF 23 JULY 1992 ON ACCESS FOR COMMUNITY AIR CARRIERS TO INTRA-COMMUNITY AIR ROUTES; 
4. FLIGHT BY THE AIRCRAFT ENGAGED IN THE SEARCH AND RESCUE OPERATIONS.
